    "text": "Given below are two statements :<br />Statement I : Ethyl pent-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-yn-oate on reaction with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>MgBr</mi></math> gives a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>-alcohol.<br />Statement II : In this reaction one mole of ethyl pent-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-yn-oate utilizes two moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>MgBr</mi></math>.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :"
